description:
USE WHEN you keep a local copy of the directory and need only what moved since your last sync (machine-readable added / updated / removed), rather than re-fetching the whole catalog.
NOT FOR a readable headline feed or one project's history (use onchain_agent_recent_changes instead), or the current state of one record (use onchain_agent_get_resource).

RETURNS (json): what changed since a given date: additions, per-resource change events, and retirements. { since, until, window_days, next_since, counts:{added,changed,removed}, added:[...], changed:[{slug,name,url,events:[...]}], removed:[...], coverage:{...}, full_export }.

CURSOR: `next_since` is the date to pass as `since` on your next call. It starts the next window at a snapshot taken before this read, so a change cannot fall between two calls; it overlaps by a couple of days, so dedupe by slug. To watch a fixed list of listings, call on a schedule with `since` = the last `next_since` and look for your slugs in each lane. A call with no argument returns a truncated sample: take the cursor from a call with `since` or detail "full", not from the sample.

COVERAGE (also stated in the response): `added` is exact. `updated` is a field-level diff of every catalog field between the snapshot on `baseline_date` and the live record — complete at daily resolution, so a quiet copy edit IS caught. `changed` is the richer event log (score moves, releases, verification) and explains WHY. `removed` is approximate. Mirror from added + updated + removed. Read-only.

WITH NO `since` (and no detail: "full") the answer is compact, labelled rule "defaulted": exact counts for the default 14-day window and the newest rows of each lane (summary: true, shown, omitted, order, example_calls). It is a sample, not a sync. Pass `since` (any date) or detail: "full" for every row; a later `since` is a shorter window and a smaller answer. All free.

Examples:
  - "what moved recently" -> {} (compact) · every row -> { detail: "full" }
  - "what's new this week" -> { since: "2026-08-23" }
  - "sync my copy" or "watch my list" -> { since: <the next_since of your last call> }
